I had the same problem.  The disk has some remnats of a partition, which 
  Linux doesn't like.  Search the web for the compaq official site on 
how to install linux.  It is for Alphaservers, but is the same for other 
models.  It gives instructions on how to use the command line 
partitioning tool.  Follow the directions, then quit, and restart linux 
install.  Use the disk wizzard, delete all the partitions on the disk, 
and use the auto-partition tool.  Then make any changes you would like 
in the wizzard.

Jeremy



