Sam <sdlarchantispam@hotmail.com> wrote:
> I ran into a similar situation.  What was happening to me was that once the
> bootstrap code was loaded, the SRM console passed all control to the OS.
> The OS didn't know about the Video console and was spitting all its output
> elsewhere.
> 
> The fix?
> 
> I established a terminal connection with the serial port to talk to the SRM
> console.

While a serial console is often of a great help, especially when
debugging troubles in a startup sequence, or capturing nasty oopses
which kill immediately everything so nothing gets logged, or when
your video goes haywire, ... in this particular case it should
be enough to type 'set console graphics' at SRM prompt (the other
option is 'set console serial').

Hitting Return key few times is usually enough to get an SRM prompt
if a console is set to serial but no serial terminal is attached.
There are reluctant cases. :-)

   Michal


