From the >>> prompt type:  sho dev
This will tell you what scsi devices you have and what they are named.
Typically device names are:
DKA0:
DKA100:
DKA200:
DKA300:
DKA400:
DKA500:

Usually (but not always) DKA0 is the primary hard drive.  Additional hard
drives are DKA100, DK200: & DKA300.  CDRoms are usually (but again not
always) designated DKA400.  Tape Drives are usually designated DKA500. DKA600
is reserved for the SCSI controller.
If you have an external SCSI plug and external SCSI devices they are usually
designated by DKB0, 100, 200., etc.

So to answer your question:, assuming that the CDRom is DKA400 and that the
actual CDRom is bootable, type:

>>>boot dka400

Good luck!

TomC


