KW <NO_SPAM_PLEASE@email.email> wrote:
> ... but in Linux it can only
> detect the first 4 hard disk, why?

The first guess would be that you have SCSI id conflicts.
Check jumpers.

The current major block number assignments in Linux reserve
a space for 128 SCSI disks, I believe (up to /dev/sddx with
a major 71).  Cases when this is limiting are likely not very
widespread.  You would need quite a few controllers to hook
all these up.

  Michal


