> How do I install and config the raid array under SuSE-Linux?

I did disconnect the DAC960, plug it into intel iron and I did run the
MS-DOS config utility. Worked fine. If you have firmware update CD-ROM's
they usually contain directory named "swcxr/utility" where you'll
find something named "RCUxxx.EXE" and that is the raid control utility. 
Copy it to floppy disk, go to ARC console and from there you can run
the program from floppy .. somehow it is also possible to start this
program via SRM but I don't know how, I've always started ARC first
and there is "run program" in one menu..

If you have DAC960 with 128kb flash, you'll need to download and flash
firmware 2.73, if bigger flash, then fw v3.51. Otherwise linux driver
will refuse to work. These fw:s are not downloadable from digital/compaq/hp
and they don't support them but downloading from mylex is ok and the
fw's seem to work fine, except that you'll need to rework your maintenance
contract :-)

