Rui Alves <code@php-db.com> wrote:
> then I do startx and I can hear
> some sound on the screen that then turns blank and after around 2
> seconds comes back to text mode with the message "fatal server error:
> Could not open default font 'fixed'".
> 
> I read somewhere that this might happen if the font server (xfs) is
> not running, but I think mine is

This may be one of reasons IF you configured your xfs in XF86Config
to use font server. Another possibiltity is to give FontPath there
explicitely instead of a socket like "unix/:7100".

Other possible reasons:
  - you did not install the font
  - you did install but a corresponding 'fonts.dir' and/or 'font.alias'
    are missing for whatever reasons
  - things are in place but the font directory is not listed either
    if config file for xfs or directly in FontPath
  - something else?

'fixed' is an alias most likely defined just at the top of
/usr/X11R6/lib/X11/fonts/misc/fonts.alias

None of the above has really very much to do with Alpha.

   Michal


