Probably, you should prepare the floppy containing the firmware update; 
it should be described in the same place you got the image, right?
As far as I know (I got the same machine), version 7.2-1 dating 
somewhere march 2000 should be the last firmware. If that's not what you 
downloaded, make sure to get firmware for Personal Workstation, or 
otherwise called 'miata'. Just follow instructions in the README.txt or 
something.

This firmware (this one image) can operate in two modes, AlphaBIOS and 
SRM. It is SRM that is most useful to you. If your machine states like 
you described, you are probable in SRM mode already. Good.

Next, read the documentation that accompanies RedHat. Make sure to read 
the Alpha specific stuff!

This newsgroup and www.alphalinux.org of www.linuxalpha.org might prove 
useful for your learning project. You are likely to come back here to 
ask about video-cards and X :-)
groups.google.com might get you going, though.

BTW, EWA0 is your ethernet device. The built-in soundcard (ESS1888) is 
not reported by 'show device'.

Good luck,

Dannis.



