Well, or example, Tru64 and Linux distros (usually) use SYSV style
startup and BSD derivatives are likely not.  So in this aspect
Tru64 and Linux are really closer.  In general both Tru64 and
Linux have "a bit of BSD, a bit of SYSV" attitude although it is
maybe more pronounced in Linux.

This request is ill-defined as it is hard to guess what Debbie
Curl really had in mind.  Linux can run Tru64 binaries (save a presence
of required libraries and for Tru64 5.x you need a bit "smarter"
kernel for that).  How closer one can get?

