Hello there.

I recall having posted about the udma-alpha-linux thingie before, 
although I can't remember the exact context. I run a heavily
patched 2.4.19 kernel on a 164SX @ 533Mhz. I've got 2x 20Gb 5400rpm 
disks booting off from a Promise U66 (PDC20262); a WD205AA, giving a
nice 21.63 MB/sec, and a ST320420A, transfering at 27.39 MB/sec. Things
do get funny though when I connect CD-Rom drives on the Promise card. 
IIRC there were known issues with the Promise controllers running CD-Rom
drives (I had seen some posts in this group. However, that was many 
_years_ ago...). As of these, I'd rather say that 15.11 MB/sec and even
33 MB/sec for a drive assumed to function as an U100 one (probably also
@7200rpm) is quite low (although it heavily depends on the disk's
characteristics). IMO you should consider recompiling your kernel and
shifting CDRom drives off from the PDC and onto your on-board controller
for stability's sake. Just a thought...

Bye,
Nick.

