> (3) 256MB SDRAM DIMMs as part of the deal.  To make a long story short,
> neither the original motherboard, nor its replacement will function with
> all three DIMMs installed!  It's rock solid if only the two outside
> sockets are populated, but will not even get to SRM if anything is in
> the middle (yes, memory has been swapped out as well.)
> 
> After carefully reviewing the manual, I'm wondering if this thing
> actually requires ECC memory.  The docs simply call for PC100 SPD
> modules.  Before I run out and spend any more money, Does anyone have a
> definitive answer?
> 
> Steve

Hey, Steven,

the vendor was fooling you a bit. The 21264 has a 128bit memory bus and 1 
SDRAM module has only 64bits, thus you need to plug in the modules in 
pairs. One module by itself won't work. If I recall correctly, when you use 
all four banks, the memory bus is 256bit wide.

Regards,

Marc


